    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, from the moment the request arrives to the moment the `201` is returned.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Authorization (before the handler runs)\n\n1. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:116`). Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise `DisableSecurityConfig` permits all.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Bean Validation of the request body (before the handler runs)\n\nTriggered by `@Valid` on the `OwnerFieldsDto` parameter (declared on the generated `OwnersApi` interface). Any failure \u2192 **400** before creation logic executes.\n\n**Field constraints (`OwnerFieldsDto`):**\n2. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n3. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n4. `title` \u2014 `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)`\n5. `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n6. `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n7. `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(max=255)`\n8. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n9. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, plus custom **`@TelephoneDigits`** (must normalize to E.164)\n10. `email` \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max=255)`\n11. `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n12. `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent`\n\n**Class-level custom validators:**\n13. **`@ValidPostcodeForCity`** \u2014 postcode must be valid for the given city (`PostcodePolicy`)\n14. **`@ValidAddressForm`** \u2014 requires a non-blank `addressLine1` *or* non-blank `address`\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Controller body (`addOwner`, lines 118\u2013135)\n\n15. **Read `Idempotency-Key` header.**\n16. **Idempotency replay check** \u2014 if this key already created an owner, return that existing owner as **200 OK** and *skip all creation entirely*.\n17. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping with normalization** (`OwnerMapperImpl.toOwner`), a side-effect on the data:\n    - `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2192 `AddressNormalizer.normalize`\n    - `address` \u2192 composed from the lines via `AddressComposer`\n    - `telephone` \u2192 normalized to E.164 (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`)\n    - `email` \u2192 lowercased (`EmailNormalizer.normalize`)\n18. Compute `sharesHousehold` flag from the DTO.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Service `createOwner` (`@Transactional`, lines 265\u2013295)\n\nBusiness validations (in order):\n\n19. **Disposable-email check** \u2014 `DisposableEmailDomains.isDisposable(email)` \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (**400**).\n20. **Assign `householdId`** \u2014 `HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode)` (side-effect).\n21. **Identity-collision check** \u2014 `rejectIdentityCollision`: among active owners with the same telephone, reject if one shares the full identity key (telephone|email|householdId) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (**409**).\n22. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 if household members already exist and `sharesHousehold` is false \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (**409**).\n23. **City-capacity check** \u2014 `countByCity \u2265 50` \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (**409**).\n24. **Set `registrationDate`** \u2014 defaults to today if absent, then adjusted to the next business day (`BusinessDayAdjuster`) (side-effect).\n25. **Daily-limit check** \u2014 `countByRegistrationDate \u2265 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n\nDerived-field side-effects assigned on the entity:\n\n26. `bulkSignupWarning` = (owners on that date > 80).\n27. `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 set by `flagPossibleDuplicate`.\n28. `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of same first+last name owners.\n29. `householdSize` \u2014 household members + 1.\n30. `customerCode` \u2014 generated and de-duplicated (`CustomerCodeGenerator`).\n\nPersistence & post-persist side-effects:\n\n31. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 persists the owner (id assigned by DB `@GeneratedValue`; no JPA `@PrePersist`/auditing callbacks; `pets` cascade not exercised since none are set here).\n32. **Audit log** \u2014 `OwnerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner)` writes an INFO line to the `\"AUDIT\"` logger.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Back in the controller\n\n33. **`idempotencyKeyRegistry.remember(key, owner.getId())`** \u2014 records the key \u2192 owner mapping in an in-memory map.\n34. **Map saved entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`** \u2014 derives many response-only fields (displayName, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, Luhn check digit, locality, timezone, etc.).\n35. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:**\n- No application events, emails, or cache eviction occur in this path.\n- The whole service method runs in a single read-write transaction; the controller itself is not transactional.\n- Response shaping for all the exceptions above lives in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail`), which affects the HTTP response but not the creation logic.\n- One easy-to-miss detail: both the `@Valid` trigger and `@PreAuthorize` are declared on the generated `OwnersApi` interface, not the controller class \u2014 reading only `OwnerRestControllerV1` would hide them."
